MUTANT {"mutant": "L334 string 'version.out' emptied", "files": [{"file": "tests/v2/test_v21_ocr_gate.py", "exit": 1, "seconds": 0.42, "outcome": "FAIL", "why": null, "ran": 1, "errors": 1, "first": "ERROR: test_a_binary_that_prints_no_version_is_never_reviewed_with (v2.test_v21_ocr_gate.Chain.test_a_binary_that_prints_no_version_is_never_reviewed_with) | aisef2.app.run.RunRefused", "tail_sha256": "edd76831e251d1ec93ff8391afe68e10dbaec0cf2b8d1b7f7f0a2cfe5bf9f0e5", "tail": "review.finder is ocr and its binary fails the identity check before the run — check declared: `<exe> version`, run alone in a clean environment, prints the pinned release and commit; expected sha256 87a165e25be69a52bb35be08705f4026f4782bf69521212e7ca43fccc5e1bf9a and a `version` line naming v1.12.12 (182898c); observed <run>/tmp/<mkdtemp>/bin/ocr: `version` could not be started (FileExistsError: [Errno 17] File exists: '<run>/tmp/aisef-ocr-version-efraje9j'). The file's bytes are the ones review.ocr.sha256 pins, but `<exe> version` did not print the version line of Open Code Review v1.12.12 (182898c); what it did instead is the observed value above (another release or commit, an error, no answer in time, no version line, or it could not be started). Run `<exe> version` yourself. If it names another release, pin the sha256 of a build of Open Code Review v1.12.12 (182898c) in review.ocr.sha256 and point review.ocr.exe at it; if it cannot be started, fails or hangs, that file does not run as the pinned release on this machine (is it executable, and built for this platform?). Or have the model review instead of Open Code Review, a different reviewer (remove review.ocr and set review.finder to \"model\"). Then run again; give it a new --out: a refused run keeps its directory as its record, and a run directory is never reused. No session was started and no provider request was sent.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 1 test\n\nFAILED (errors=1)\n", "overhead_s